bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    textarea_4x_device_height_not_in_ancestor_2026-11-27, 0, "At device scale 4 Chrome 159 lays a rows=10 textarea (13.333px monospace, padding 0, border 0) out 630 device px tall (157.5 CSS, 1x: 150) with a 63 px line pitch, and an auto-height overflow:hidden wrapper (padding-bottom:1px) grows with it to 634. Simple keeps the CSS box at 150, paints the textarea taller through its device-extra-height, but the wrapper stays at 4 x 151 = 604 and its clip cuts the textarea there; Simple's value line pitch is 60 device px."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    textarea_4x_device_height_not_in_ancestor_2026-11-27, P3, closed, "stale: FIXED by p3sweep-20261127 (auto-height block parent now records the lowest in-flow block child device bottom incl box_device_extra_h, so textarea/select device-height deltas propagate to the auto-height ancestor); AC-7/AC-8 of textarea_value_clip_chrome159_spec PASS 2026-11-27. Was: 4x textarea device height delta is not carried by its auto-height ancestor", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_engine.spl, 2006, "AUTO_WRAP_PAGE in test/01_unit/browser_engine/textarea_value_clip_chrome159_spec.spl at k=4: Chrome yellow strip rows 630-633, Simple none (textarea white to 603, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    textarea_4x_device_height_not_in_ancestor_2026-11-27, 0, "2026-11-27 webrender-textarea-clip Linux aarch64 seed cargo-target-wr-seed1126b (sha256 fb80903917d6d5f5), Chrome for Testing 159.0.8154.6 --force-device-scale-factor=4 --hide-scrollbars, 400x300: Chrome textarea rows 0-629, wrapper strip 630-633, next block 634. Simple: textarea background to 603, next block 604. The block path records box_device_extra_h only from the cursor fraction (layout_engine.spl ~5558), so a child form control's device extra never reaches the parent. Paint clamps the textarea's grown clip edge to the wrapper's applied edge (_html_draw_ir_far_edge_delta), so nothing paints past 604."
    textarea_4x_device_height_not_in_ancestor_2026-11-27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: reproduced AUTO_WRAP_PAGE at k=4 per the SDN record: textarea painted to row 600, wrapper strip 600-603, body from 604 - device-height delta never reached the parent. Root cause: the block-path bottom record set box_device_extra_h only from the box's own cursor fraction; a block-level form control child's recorded device extra (box_device_extra_h_at, from form_control_device_extra_h) never propagated to the auto-height parent, so paint clamped the child clip edge to the wrapper's un-grown edge. Fix (layout_engine.spl): track the lowest in-flow block child's CSS bottom and device bottom in the child loop; at the record, an auto-height box whose cursor bottom is that child's bottom records the signed carry (textarea grows +E, select shrinks -2 at k=4), matching Chrome. Spec textarea_value_clip_chrome159_spec extended: AC-7 pins the strip invariant on face-set hosts; AC-8 (select in auto-height wrapper, target 66 = 4x17-2) discriminates on every host - both PASS; target spec 5/8 with AC-2/3/5 failing identically to pre-fix baseline (environmental font metrics, this Windows host has no measured Linux face set). Neighbours overflow_hidden_fractional_clip_4x 4/4 PASS; other textarea specs match baselines. Residual: floated form controls (BFC CSS-px only) remain, out of minimal scope; recommend a Linux lane re-run for the full Chrome-exact rows. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/browser_engine/textarea_value_clip_chrome159_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/browser_engine/overflow_hidden_fractional_clip_4x_chrome159_spec.spl"

bug_fix_strategies |bug_id, line_num, content|
    textarea_4x_device_height_not_in_ancestor_2026-11-27, 0, "Either carry the child control's device extra into the parent's device bottom (and the clip edge it owns), or size the textarea in device-scaled line metrics so its CSS height is 157.5 at k=4 like Chrome. Pin with the AUTO_WRAP_PAGE strip rows 630-633 and the 63 px pitch."

